      "evidence": "template/scripts/machine_pool.py read_holders: `if _try_lock(fd, path, shared=True): fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)`. _try_take_slots uses LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB on the same slot files. _scan_queue(remove_dead=False) takes the same kind of shared lock on tickets.",
      "id": "holder-probe-contends-with-acquire",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The read-only holder probe (status and the waiting report) takes a shared flock on each slot file. A concurrent head's non-blocking exclusive attempt on that slot can fail spuriously, so a free token looks busy until the next poll. The spec requires read-only status and all-or-nothing acquisition, and the result is only a delayed admission, not a contract violation."
